Source: armcb-isp-v4l2-dkms
Maintainer: ISP Driver Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Standards-Version: 4.5.1
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 12), rsync

Package: armcb-isp-v4l2-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 2.1.0.0)
Recommends: build-essential, linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-arm64
Description: ARM Cambricon ISP V4L2 driver (DKMS source)
 V4L2 driver for the CIX SoC ISP / camera subsystem (armcb_isp_v4l2.ko).
 .
 This package ships only source code — DKMS compiles the module on the
 target board against the running kernel, and rebuilds automatically on
 kernel upgrade. Although architecture-independent, the source itself
 only supports aarch64 + CIX SoC at runtime.
